msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:145
msgid "The path to the initramfs."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:149 src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:157
#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:175 src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:213
#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:236
msgid ""
"If the path is relative, it is relative to the manifest's enclosing "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:151
msgid ""
"Grub options. Only take effect if boot method is `grub-rescue-iso` or `grub-"
"qcow2`."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:153
msgid "The path to the `grub-mkrescue` executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:155 src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:173
msgid ""
"Optional. The default value is the executable in the system path, if any."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:159
msgid "The protocol GRUB used."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:161
msgid "Optional. The default value is `multiboot2`."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:163
msgid "Possible values are `linux`, `multiboot`, and `multiboot2`."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:165
msgid "Whether to display the GRUB menu when booting with GRUB."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:169
msgid "Options for finding and starting QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:171
msgid "The path to the QEMU executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:177
msgid ""
"Additional arguments passed to QEMU are organized in a single string that "
"can include any POSIX shell compliant separators."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:182
msgid ""
"Each argument should be in the form of `KEY` and `VALUE` or `KEY` if no "
"value is required. Some keys can appear multiple times (e.g., `-device`, `-"
"netdev`), while other keys can appear at most once. Certain keys, such as `-"
"kernel` and `-initrd`, are not allowed to be set here as they may conflict "
"with the settings of OSDK."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:191
msgid ""
"The field will be evaluated, so it is ok to use environment variables in the "
"arguments (usually for paths or conditional arguments). You can even use "
"this mechanism to read from files by using command replacement `$(cat path/"
"to/your/custom/args/file)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:196
msgid "The path to the file where QEMU writes the guest output."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:198
msgid ""
"Optional. If this field is absent, OSDK does not inspect QEMU output for "
"kernel panics or coverage data."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:202
msgid ""
"This field only tells OSDK where to read the log; it does not cause QEMU to "
"create the file. QEMU must be configured through `args` to write guest "
"output to the same path. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:207
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[qemu]\n"
"args = \"-serial file:qemu-serial.log\"\n"
"log_file = \"qemu-serial.log\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:216
msgid "The `with_daemons` host processes to run for the duration of QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:218
msgid ""
"Optional. If this field is absent or is an empty array (`[]`), OSDK does not "
"spawn any daemons."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:221
msgid "Each daemon has a `path` and an optional list of `args` passed to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:223
msgid ""
"OSDK stops each daemon after QEMU exits if it has not already terminated. If "
"a daemon exits unsuccessfully while QEMU is running, OSDK terminates QEMU "
"and reports an execution error. A daemon that exits successfully is reaped "
"and does not abort the run. During shutdown, OSDK sends `SIGTERM` to each "
"daemon's process group and sends `SIGKILL` after five seconds if it is still "
"running. OSDK waits one second after starting each daemon before continuing "
"QEMU setup. A managed daemon must remain in the foreground for its entire "
"lifetime; it must not fork into the background after startup. These daemons "
"are intended for processes tied to QEMU's lifecycle. For one-shot processes, "
"manage them in your own scripts instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:239
msgid ""
"Special settings for running. Only take effect when running `cargo osdk run`."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:241
msgid "By default, it inherits common options."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:243
msgid "Values set here are used to override common options."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:245
msgid "Special settings for testing."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:247
msgid "Similar to `22`, but only take effect when running `cargo osdk test`."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:249
msgid "The definition of customized scheme."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:251
msgid ""
"A customized scheme has the same fields as the default scheme. By default, a "
"customized scheme will inherit all options from the default scheme, unless "
"overridden by new options."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:255
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:257
msgid ""
"Here is a sound, self-explanatory example which is used by OSDK in the "
"Asterinas project."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:260
msgid ""
"In the script `./tools/qemu_args.sh`, the environment variables will be used "
"to determine the actual set of qemu arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:263
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# The OSDK manifest at the Asterinas root virtual workspace\n"
"# provides default OSDK settings for all packages.\n"
"\n"
"# The common options for build, run and test\n"
"[boot]\n"
"method = \"grub-rescue-iso\"\n"
"\n"
"[grub]\n"
"boot_protocol = \"multiboot2\"\n"
"\n"
"[qemu]\n"
"args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh normal)\"\n"
"log_file = \"qemu-serial.log\"\n"
"\n"
"# Special options for running\n"
"[run.boot]\n"
"kcmd_args = [\n"
"    \"SHELL=/bin/sh\",\n"
"    \"LOGNAME=root\",\n"
"    \"HOME=/\",\n"
"    \"USER=root\",\n"
"    \"PATH=/bin:/benchmark\",\n"
"]\n"
"init_args = [\"sh\", \"-l\"]\n"
"\n"
"# Special options for testing\n"
"[test.qemu]\n"
"args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh test)\"\n"
"\n"
"# Other Schemes\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"microvm\"]\n"
"boot.method = \"vmm-direct\"\n"
"build.strip_elf = true\n"
"qemu.args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh microvm)\"\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"iommu\"]\n"
"supported_archs = [\"x86_64\"]\n"
"qemu.args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh iommu)\"\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"tdx\"]\n"
"supported_archs = [\"x86_64\"]\n"
"build.features = [\"cvm_guest\"]\n"
"boot.method = \"grub-qcow2\"\n"
"grub.boot_protocol = \"linux\"\n"
"qemu.args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh tdx)\"\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"riscv\"]\n"
"supported_archs = [\"riscv64\"]\n"
"boot.method = \"vmm-direct\"\n"
"build.strip_elf = false\n"
"qemu.args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh riscv)\"\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"sifive_u\"]\n"
"supported_archs = [\"riscv64\"]\n"
"build.features = [\"riscv_sv39_mode\"]\n"
"boot.method = \"vmm-direct\"\n"
"build.strip_elf = false\n"
"qemu.with_monitor = true\n"
"\n"
"qemu.args = \"\"\"\\\n"
"    -machine sifive_u \\\n"
"    -m 8G \\\n"
"    -smp 5 \\\n"
"    -no-reboot \\\n"
"    -nographic \\\n"
"    -display none \\\n"
"    -serial chardev:mux \\\n"
"    -monitor chardev:mux \\\n"
"    -chardev stdio,id=mux,mux=on,signal=off,logfile=qemu.log\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"loongarch\"]\n"
"boot.method = \"vmm-direct\"\n"
"build.strip_elf = false\n"
"\n"
"qemu.args = \"\"\"\\\n"
"    -machine virt \\\n"
"    -m 8G \\\n"
"    -smp 1 \\\n"
"    --no-reboot \\\n"
"    -nographic \\\n"
"    -display none \\\n"
"    -serial chardev:mux \\\n"
"    -monitor chardev:mux \\\n"
"    -chardev stdio,id=mux,mux=on,signal=off,logfile=qemu.log \\\n"
"    -device virtio-keyboard-pci \\\n"
"    -device virtio-serial \\\n"
"    -device virtconsole,chardev=mux \\\n"
"    -rtc base=utc\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"[scheme.\"aarch64\"]\n"
"supported_archs = [\"aarch64\"]\n"
"boot.method = \"vmm-direct\"\n"
"build.strip_elf = false\n"
"qemu.args = \"$(./tools/qemu_args.sh aarch64)\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:363
msgid "Scheme"
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:365
msgid ""
"Scheme is an advanced feature that allows you to create multiple profiles "
"for the same action (`build`, `run`, or `test`) under different scenarios (e."
"g., x86 vs. RISC-V). Schemes support any user-defined keys (see the 23rd "
"configuration) and can be selected using the `--scheme` CLI argument."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:370
msgid ""
"If a scheme `<s>` is selected for an action (such as `test`), the value of "
"an unspecified but required configuration `key` will be determined by the "
"following rules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:373
msgid ""
"If the general config (`scheme.<s>.key`) exists for the selected scheme, use "
"this value."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:375
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if the default scheme has this configuration for the action "
"(`test.key`), use this value."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:377
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if the default scheme has this configuration (`key`), use this "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: src/osdk/reference/manifest.md:380
msgid ""
"If the value is still not found, either the default value for the key will "
"be used or an error will be thrown."
msgstr ""
